                <pb facs="0489" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 16948/23.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to the embassy’s telegram of the 9th, Mr. Adee informs Mr. Thompson
                    that the department is to-day forwarding by mail a memorandum discussing the
                    Rodriguez case, and directs him to make formal request for provisional detention
                    under treaty in usual way, if and when Rodriguez is released on amparo.</p>
            </div>
